{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 3D Gaussian Splatting from Scratch Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: A 2D Gaussian"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "We first build a 2D rasteriser. The 3D case reduces to it after projection."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn.functional as F"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def eval_2d_gaussian(means, covs, points):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    means:  (G, 2)      centres"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    covs:   (G, 2, 2)   covariance matrices"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    points: (H, W, 2)   pixel coordinates"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    returns: (G, H, W)  density at every pixel for every Gaussian"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    G = means.size(0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    H, W, _ = points.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    flat = points.view(-1, 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    inv = torch.linalg.inv(covs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    diff = flat[None, :, :] - means[:, None, :]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    d = torch.einsum(\"gpi,gij,gpj->gp\", diff, inv, diff)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    density = torch.exp(-0.5 * d)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return density.view(G, H, W)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`einsum` does the quadratic form `diff^T Sigma^-1 diff` for every (Gaussian, pixel) pair."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: 2D splatting rasteriser"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Alpha-compositing front-to-back. Depth in 2D is meaningless, so we use a learned per-Gaussian scalar for order."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def rasterise_2d(means, covs, colours, opacities, depths, image_size):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    means:     (G, 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    covs:      (G, 2, 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    colours:   (G, 3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    opacities: (G,)     in [0, 1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    depths:    (G,)     per-Gaussian scalar used for ordering"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    image_size: (H, W)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    returns:   (H, W, 3) rendered image"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    H, W = image_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    yy, xx = torch.meshgrid("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        torch.arange(H, dtype=torch.float32, device=means.device),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        torch.arange(W, dtype=torch.float32, device=means.device),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        indexing=\"ij\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    points = torch.stack([xx, yy], dim=-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    densities = eval_2d_gaussian(means, covs, points)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    alphas = opacities[:, None, None] * densities"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    alphas = alphas.clamp(0.0, 0.99)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    order = torch.argsort(depths)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    alphas = alphas[order]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    colours_sorted = colours[order]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    T = torch.ones(H, W, device=means.device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    out = torch.zeros(H, W, 3, device=means.device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(means.size(0)):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        a = alphas[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        out += (T * a)[..., None] * colours_sorted[i][None, None, :]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        T = T * (1.0 - a)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return out"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Not fast \u2014 a real implementation uses tile-based CUDA kernels \u2014 but exactly the right math and fully differentiable."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: A trainable 2D splat scene"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class Splats2D(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, num_splats=128, image_size=64, seed=0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        g = torch.Generator().manual_seed(seed)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        H, W = image_size, image_size"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.means = nn.Parameter(torch.rand(num_splats, 2, generator=g) * torch.tensor([W, H]))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.log_scale = nn.Parameter(torch.ones(num_splats, 2) * math.log(2.0))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.rot = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(num_splats))  # single angle in 2D"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.colour_logits = nn.Parameter(torch.randn(num_splats, 3, generator=g) * 0.5)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.opacity_logit = nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(num_splats))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.depth = nn.Parameter(torch.rand(num_splats, generator=g))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def covs(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        s = torch.exp(self.log_scale)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        c, si = torch.cos(self.rot), torch.sin(self.rot)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        R = torch.stack(["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            torch.stack([c, -si], dim=-1),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            torch.stack([si, c], dim=-1),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ], dim=-2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        S = torch.diag_embed(s ** 2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return R @ S @ R.transpose(-1, -2)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, image_size):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        covs = self.covs()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        colours = torch.sigmoid(self.colour_logits)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        opacities = torch.sigmoid(self.opacity_logit)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return rasterise_2d(self.means, covs, colours, opacities, self.depth, image_size)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`log_scale`, `opacity_logit`, and `colour_logits` are all unconstrained parameters mapped through the right activation at render time. This is the standard pattern for every 3DGS implementation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Fit 2D Gaussians to a target image"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def make_target(size=64):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    yy, xx = np.meshgrid(np.arange(size), np.arange(size), indexing=\"ij\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    img = np.zeros((size, size, 3), dtype=np.float32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    # Red circle"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mask = (xx - 20) ** 2 + (yy - 20) ** 2 < 10 ** 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    img[mask] = [1.0, 0.2, 0.2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    # Blue square"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mask = (np.abs(xx - 45) < 8) & (np.abs(yy - 40) < 8)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    img[mask] = [0.2, 0.3, 1.0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return torch.from_numpy(img)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "target = make_target(64)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = Splats2D(num_splats=64, image_size=64)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "opt = torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=0.05)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for step in range(200):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    pred = model((64, 64))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss = F.mse_loss(pred, target)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    opt.zero_grad(); loss.backward(); opt.step()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if step % 40 == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"step {step:3d}  mse {loss.item():.4f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Over 200 steps the 64 Gaussians settle into the two shapes. That is the entire idea \u2014 gradient-descent on explicit geometric primitives."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: From 2D to 3D"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The 3D extension keeps the same loop. The additions:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "1. Per-Gaussian rotation is a quaternion instead of a single angle."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "2. Covariance is `R S S^T R^T` with `R` built from the quaternion and `S = diag(exp(log_scale))`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "3. Projection `(mu, Sigma) -> (mu', Sigma')` uses the camera extrinsics and the Jacobian of the perspective projection at `mu`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "4. Colour becomes a spherical-harmonics expansion; evaluate it at the viewing direction."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "5. Depth-sort is from actual camera-space z instead of a learned scalar."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Every production implementation (`gsplat`, `inria/gaussian-splatting`, `nerfstudio`) does exactly this on the GPU with tile-based CUDA kernels."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: Spherical harmonics evaluation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The SH basis up to degree 3 has 16 terms per channel. Evaluation:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def eval_sh_degree_3(sh_coeffs, dirs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sh_coeffs: (..., 16, 3)   last dim is RGB channels"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    dirs:      (..., 3)       unit vectors"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    returns:   (..., 3)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    C0 = 0.282094791773878"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    C1 = 0.488602511902920"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    C2 = [1.092548430592079, 1.092548430592079,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "          0.315391565252520, 1.092548430592079,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "          0.546274215296039]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x, y, z = dirs[..., 0], dirs[..., 1], dirs[..., 2]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x2, y2, z2 = x * x, y * y, z * z"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    xy, yz, xz = x * y, y * z, x * z"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    result = C0 * sh_coeffs[..., 0, :]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    result = result - C1 * y[..., None] * sh_coeffs[..., 1, :]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    result = result + C1 * z[..., None] * sh_coeffs[..., 2, :]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    result = result - C1 * x[..., None] * sh_coeffs[..., 3, :]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    result = result + C2[0] * xy[..., None] * sh_coeffs[..., 4, :]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    result = result + C2[1] * yz[..., None] * sh_coeffs[..., 5, :]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    result = result + C2[2] * (2.0 * z2 - x2 - y2)[..., None] * sh_coeffs[..., 6, :]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    result = result + C2[3] * xz[..., None] * sh_coeffs[..., 7, :]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    result = result + C2[4] * (x2 - y2)[..., None] * sh_coeffs[..., 8, :]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    # degree 3 terms omitted here for brevity; full 16-coefficient version in the code file"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return result"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Learned `sh_coeffs` store the \"colour in every direction\" for that Gaussian. At render time you evaluate against the current view direction and get a 3-vector RGB."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Run the 2D splat trainer above on a different synthetic image. Vary `num_splats` in `[16, 64, 256]` and plot MSE vs step for each. Identify the point of diminishing returns.\n2. **(Medium)** Extend the 2D rasteriser to support per-Gaussian RGB colours that depend on a scalar \"view angle\" through a degree-2 harmonic. Train on a pair of target images and verify the model reconstructs both.\n3. **(Hard)** Clone `nerfstudio` and train `splatfacto` on a 20-photo capture of any scene you have (desk, plant, face, room). Export to glTF `KHR_gaussian_splatting` and open it in a viewer (Three.js `GaussianSplats3D`, SuperSplat, Babylon.js V9). Report training time, number of Gaussians, and rendered fps."
      ]
    }
  ],
